# {{.project_name}}

Production-shaped Android app generated by smokeforge.

## Stack

- Kotlin with AGP 9.5 built-in Kotlin support
- Jetpack Compose, Material 3, Navigation Compose
- Hilt + KSP
- Retrofit + OkHttp + kotlinx.serialization
- DataStore with Android Keystore-backed encrypted tokens
- Gradle Kotlin DSL, version catalog, wrapper, and build-logic convention plugins
- Compile SDK 37.1, target SDK 37, min SDK 26, JDK 17

## Commands

```bash
./gradlew test
./gradlew lint
./gradlew assembleDebug
```

Or use `make test`, `make lint`, `make build`, and `make ci`.

## Built-in behaviour

- Email/password sign-in, registration, password-reset request, refresh rotation,
  logout, and current-account loading against the smokeforge API.
- Debug cleartext is limited to local development. Staging and release builds
  should point at HTTPS endpoints.
- Staging and release API URLs can be overridden with
  `-PstagingApiBaseUrl=...` and `-PreleaseApiBaseUrl=...`.
- Release builds enable R8 and resource shrinking. Signing is read from:
  `SMOKE_KEYSTORE_PATH`, `SMOKE_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD`, `SMOKE_KEY_ALIAS`, and
  `SMOKE_KEY_PASSWORD`.
- No tokens, passwords, or authorization headers are logged.

## Code layout

```text
app/                  Application, activity, root navigation, app wiring
build-logic/          Android application/library/Compose/Hilt conventions
core/common/          Pure result, error, and dispatcher contracts
core/model/           Pure domain models and repository interfaces
core/designsystem/    Material 3 theme and shared components
core/network/         Retrofit APIs, DTOs, and RFC 9457 error mapping
core/datastore/       DataStore settings and encrypted token storage
core/data/            Repositories, session policy, interceptors, Hilt modules
core/testing/         Fakes and test data
feature/auth/         Sign-in, registration, and password reset
feature/home/         API status and account summary
feature/settings/     Appearance, environment, and sign-out
```

